# See packages/extract/.npmignore for why this file must exist (even
# near-empty) for `pnpm deploy` to include dist/ output: an absent
# .npmignore falls back to the root .gitignore's blanket `dist/` rule,
# which would silently drop the build output.
#
# packaging/ is excluded explicitly: it holds this package's own build
# scripts and (once built) their dist/ output — macOS/Windows SEA
# binaries, zips, and the Linux tarball itself — none of which belong
# inside a deploy of @nia/agent's runtime. Root .gitignore's `dist/` rule
# would normally keep packaging/*/dist out, but that rule doesn't apply
# here (see above), so without this line a deploy recursively bundles
# every previously-built platform package — this is what took the Linux
# tarball from ~13 MB to ~180 MB.
packaging/
